How can we introduce the concept of addition to students with special needs using everyday objects and visual representations?To introduce addition to students with special needs, we can use everyday objects and visual representations:

* Everyday objects: Use toys or blocks to represent numbers. Show students how adding toys together by physically combining them results in a larger collection.
