magnitude = sqrt(x^2 + y^2 + z^2)

Your program should prompt the user to enter the values of x, y, and z, which must be positive integers between 1 and 100, inclusive. Then, calculate and display the magnitude of the vector using the formula.

Example:
Enter the value of x (1-100): 57
Enter the value of y (1-100): 89
