7. To plot the point (-1, -1), we start at the point (0, 0) and move 1 unit to the left and 1 unit down.
8. Continue plotting points until you have a good representation of the function.
9. Connect the points with a smooth curve.

The graph of the function y = x is a straight line that passes through the origin and has a slope of 1.
